  "notes": "⛔ **This model is the pop side, deliberately, and it is the only entry in this batch that is not half-time.** The research gives two lanes — \"88–104 straight (2&4) on the pop singles, 140–150 half-time on the rap cuts\" — and rates the pop-structural habits as the clearly documented half while calling the trap-side detail lighter. So `session.halfTime` is false, `snare.placement` is `backbeat_24`, and the tempo band is 88–104. The trap-side cuts are exactly the parent archetype and are not restated here; what makes B.o.B worth a model inside a trap roster is the half that is *not* trap. ⛔ **The one entry in this batch that grows a real bass part.** \"Alternates real electric-bass lines (pop side) with tuned 808 (rap side)\" is `bass808.role: counter_riff` — which is what stops `bass::generate` returning an empty lane — plus a `bassline` block playing `independent_riff` with a 17-semitone reach and `followRootsProb` 0.62, because a guitar-derived pop record has a bass that moves rather than one that mirrors the kick. Its register tops out at 45 against a chord floor of 50, so the bass cannot sit above its own harmony. \"Guitar-derived voicings mean real IV–V motion rather than static vamps\" is why the families are all four-chord and major, why `harmonicRhythm` never reaches `vamp`, and why the arrangement is verse–prechorus–chorus rather than loop-and-hook — the only structure in this batch with a pre-chorus. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium`: the research rates this high-medium and says the trap-side detail is lighter. INFERRED: every velocity figure, the `tambourine` density standing in for \"tambourine 8ths\", the `passingTones` set (restricted to `P5`/`M2`/`M6`, all diatonic in a major key, so the walked notes are harmony rather than chromatic approach), and the whole `intervals`/`contour` split. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.55 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.55 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub.",
